# Performance of the sorting example

Requirements on `examples/sort.deus`, checked by `deus mdl`. Costs are machine steps, so each
verdict is reproducible on any machine and either kernel.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                        |
| ------ | -------------------------- |
| `perf` | `org.dxos.deus.perf@1.0`   |

## Requirements

Insertion sort is quadratic on reversed input (each element walks the whole sorted prefix):

```mdl
perf P-1: insertion sort is quadratic on reversed input
  run: fun n => Sort.isort (List.reverse (List.range 0 n))
  sizes: 20 | 40 | 80
  order: n^2
  budget: 100000
```

and linear on sorted input, where each insert stops at once:

```mdl
perf P-2: insertion sort is linear on sorted input
  run: fun n => Sort.isort (List.range 0 n)
  sizes: 20 | 40 | 80
  order: n
```

A single run within a budget:

```mdl
perf P-3: sorting ten numbers
  run: Sort.isort [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6, 5, 3]
  budget: 2000
```
